From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] The TrimUI Brick stays off when a charger is plugged in: the
 PMIC powers on for it whatever the boot loader says, so when the cable was
 the only reason (REG 20 says why), it powers off again at once and the
 battery charges with the Brick off

---
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -612,6 +612,20 @@
 		 * so it is set here at every boot for the next power-on.
 		 */
 		pmic_bus_write(0x26, 0x1c);
+		/*
+		 * Plugging in a charger powers the Brick on: the PMIC's factory
+		 * setting, which no register changes. When the cable was the only
+		 * reason this time (REG 20: bit 2 VBUS insert, bit 0 the power key;
+		 * 0 after a restart, which isn't a power-on), it powers off again
+		 * (REG 27 bit 0), and the battery charges with the Brick off.
+		 */
+		u8 source;
+
+		if (!pmic_bus_read(0x20, &source) && (source & 0x05) == 0x04) {
+			pmic_bus_setbits(0x27, 0x01);
+			for (;;)
+				;
+		}
 	}
 #endif
 
